eted' : filter !== 'Deleted')\\n        : filter !== 'Deleted';\\n      if (scope === 'Active' && eligibleFilter && ['0', '1'].includes(value)) {\\n        transaction(() => {\\n          const tasks = matchingDirectoryTasks(scope, filter, prioritySelection, range, query);\\n          for (const task of tasks) {\\n            if (deletion) {\\n              setTaskDeleted.run(Number(value), task.id, task.project_id);\\n            } else if (task.completed !== Number(value)) {\\n              updateTask.run(Number(value), task.id, task.project_id);\\n            }\\n          }\\n        });\\n      }\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":684,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_04013dc4bc97c6a3016acbd85ca6ac81939d142310108706f3","object":"response","created_at":1791744092,"completed_at":1791744105,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_04013dc4bc97c6a3016acbd85dc2fc8193a8d6c7830558cca6","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Refining route management**\n\nI'll work on implementing a shared route completion or deletion process to reduce duplication while keeping the existing routes intact. It’s important to ensure comprehensive tests are in place, so I’ll set up a new file for this purpose. I'll need to use a fixture to import database snapshots and potentially restart the moves. This way, we can maintain efficiency and ensure everything runs smoothly. Let’s make sure we cover all bases!"}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqy9hf_xUzGRyGMhW6Fl5WTSoh7GlLtBgCqP4gZP4NyeqrRzApWWP_agbLLUfRXvw0pmINEJSx8dqUri-bbF4ApUTL9tCJBViQ70buzgN7Eq7kXIO0rspvfvwK85kWE51w97wnlIL9MHZL93Mo5QFDBsWPuTOJbQ_NL-6W63wD9rTD0t14x1FY3SZSiv7BOyIsy7cTVkJA2npURUiLebNsTW_s0to5TlHnqwL19fuPUvaVJxIBQKuurcmBPucUyMAVx-ds-yoYo46UqkG_rP_8TR_nHcnxDMsQkQ6OjxUyomdE79JDB9j2UzNt9yKYn19b6bwS2XgmkvzckRUdFchrCb_OfD2riUWppB7C_zeK9TeP_8IpEW5fjdqfAF0nv2CV_RRztdbtQOv7nnygGIev6hjJyMDN0kQIR3rTaC8FmeR6ynx0XUp7uNShfucAQBfzR5Y7WxdONq-H-F4la2GffWtgfEPsj_vrXfjXd6UMf4kb4BQn7h-8J921_Ny7znD-sIlDdOoSn0TbdJ6N2LK1Uj6-S2kZwIpJiGptrLCBSGFWpUJAV1Zo1CiqNdZ0JDNFY6s9GxVwaEn1Ko-LxIaUNByI9wZ7u1H05Nq9WuMPymFf1HPb7THuSrnuDw7s6Br6eZoIEcyzP326U_wSsK7kmxLCKiov1o0NvrktHPlt4n_iCOMkzxbI_zI226rgOyg0osRhqsfywTYC9tMUpGw22e1Jy8O87XTKvofurdLgkSvInh8Rhz1PeBvNNu-9UbQ0eXNjoTQDasiqTKgYpxnYHTP-M7XiuUMjXNLA1cvw6BQBGRZGCSTY8b-Q5U8egn_O3HQ4ErzRE5xL8Cem_oCQySSKJCvIG7UtH9Q1yoE5GIkI-ZEv9t3KzBTBu-3wWL-9G2x7yvpWv9tN7jKrg6SK80BSlGFmKXfqayWJ4T8S_UTc0t1iI3hPPqktptFy7IPtu7EyEnX70O_4ljfXIxxmhY9XQMopAxS-yjITJPJIG9dWO_mY9yg73mdc0nt5sSOQgDM7fZEz9hxGVLJbJQ3o5p5sIao_T_23zpWpIM7kWbYMa4LvSQR1DULiNkJ0F5Z0BM3V20Lz_sfDR06X5iOWlJRN3xgvLxuDbL_8i6lJ7ojtGEvNjz0AMtImYGL91XGnFBY75f_zuOs3C7lyvHYZlc1SvI54VxmKNkzw1ypwX04U4ztK4ISEKMb6MCr0EvgdNy73t2PPfnsP4aLRahTbkQvMvmRU3QbPLY36aEANth7N0ivLeqgouWtnigPSiP7qY9tDPwmN3J0dyaqf8CgzS9TiwmOye83xKxMA7j6DuU0SVDte_BvRZJpY3dFDZNq4-9uFS_OKmMqBY8zIidajr3CVhUQc0SJQ2jzC4iBzB8nTgHY5aNMvJH_tT8A4P4-G7TYhXxJjRa7MPLuD0ipmXQ_e9KPZ0v0PznFWwYxUMBpPCCCl-k2fHknwEhgBnSQ4X3cfb5He7WHHpKzh9VAj7sB5k_Hj-sIuObaAYJUnMwhf7VXdAZRE1_8Tqeh768HVNGFrHHF2GU45kLAMgZ44u2qWWmxRKm3IRJAFkddz2FUG8Ekh2te7ux2GZWCCwzi8BcwdkJiZPEqg9kWWcCXOvWGoLfozNfPX7QTg4Fbz8z2jvuL4t71GPe9YEU4ew2rvJkvx9Uiduq1-QyGYAqUsIzU0WD96b_daU86IG1j2BjFD1BBSW-3fY2i5C4BXiLZtaRouQOd9QJ70zCDNFVwISAc4nBu8-gTG9JZLtm-yYDBiurBGXGMnO3SIOXdtS_12gtMJs8aJE4J7VI6byADWp9X9XrJH_n9rS6LKEzsRG9ksm_8UbAO4eX5HQ_Yqd65A_QRvZajETQ-hsEyaFGsmepLNp0Zog06FcH_VJt-Km9c4hk4Ai7anXN5FHeCrWR7AJv9uWHAqYWl6vEkav